{
  "about": [
    "The connection lines the Windows installer and Show-RpaConnection.ps1 print, one per program, for the Connection Line field of the RPA Desktop Runner and RPA Browser credentials. The installer's Pester tests and the node's tests read this file.",
    "rpa-runner://<address>:<port>/rpa/v1#token=<token>&fingerprint=<64 hex> and rpa-browser://<address>:<port>/#token=<token>&fingerprint=<64 hex>. An IPv6 address is in brackets. The fingerprint is the SHA-256 of the certificate as 64 lower-case hexadecimal digits, without colons. The token is the installer's own (letters, digits, - and _), as it is.",
    "url is the URL that the line stands for, as the separate URL line prints it. Without -ShowTokens the token is the placeholder in hiddenToken, which is not a token: a credential refuses such a line.",
    "Every token and fingerprint here is made up for these tests; none is a secret."
  ],
  "hiddenToken": "<hidden: run with -ShowTokens>",
